      "content": "hey so i've been doing some solo sessions with my modular synth and i've noticed something weird. whenever i hit this specific set of dissonant intervals—basically a cluster of minor seconds layered over a Tritone—something actually happens in the room. like, the glass water on my desk starts showing these perfect Faraday wave patterns even though the sub is barely moving. i've recorded the waveform and it feels like the frequency is interacting with the local field in a way that standard acoustics doesn't explain. help me figure out the math behind this?",
