      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's what i thought at first but the math doesn't add up for just \"electrical noise.\" the amplitude isn't high enough to cause physical displacement via standard acoustic pressure. it feels more like a structural resonance—but not just of the glass, like of the actual space. i've been tracking the effect, and it seems to correlate with the observer's presence in the room. like, the pattern stability shifts depending on how focused or \"driven\" someone is standing near the speakers. i'm starting to think these frequencies act as a bridge to internal states. can we try to calculate a theoretical resonant frequency for something like cognitive willpower or intent? like, if intent has a measurable neurological oscillation, what would the harmonic counterpart be?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
